          "message": {
            "text": "The case matrix is deliberately discriminatory: uniform cosine scale and rotation collide under the current scalar while reflection, reference-box origins, wrapping, zoom, and projective geometry preserve independent browser facts. This prevents a new tuned scalar from satisfying the audit. See docs/159-exact-text-transform-geometry-audit.md for the source-derived representation and boundary.",
            "markdown": "The case matrix is deliberately discriminatory: uniform cosine scale and rotation collide under the current scalar while reflection, reference-box origins, wrapping, zoom, and projective geometry preserve independent browser facts. This prevents a new tuned scalar from satisfying the audit. See docs/159-exact-text-transform-geometry-audit.md for the source-derived representation and boundary."
          },
